# PA0: take production down so the cards are free. PRODUCTION IS LIVE ON THE CARDS when this window opens (the node agent's serving
# container holds all four boards), so the FIRST job of the window stops the agent (agentstop: the agent, and with it the serving container
# it started) and then anything else still serving (unserve). No board is opened, no image is built, no reset runs: that is P2's.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-3-prof window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-3-prof and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig,
# a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG is required by the parser and names the image P2 builds; PA0 does not use it.
# Pass: the status step lists every board and the agent's container is gone. Stop rule: any failure stops the window (and then the cards are
# handed back with PH only if the agent was stopped; if it was not, nothing was taken and nothing needs handing back).
# Duration (estimate): 5 min.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status agentstop unserve
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prof-2
